</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">How should personal data be handled in content created for AI optimization?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Personal data should be excluded from AEO-optimized content unless specifically necessary. When required, implement pseudonymization techniques, obtain appropriate consent, and ensure data minimization compliance.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">Are there specific privacy requirements for schema markup in AEO?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Schema markup has no specific regulatory requirements but must comply with general privacy principles. Avoid including personal data in structured data formats that may be easily processed by AI engines.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">What records must be maintained for AEO privacy compliance?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Organizations must maintain data processing documentation, consent records, vendor agreements, privacy impact assessments, and audit trails for data access and modifications.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">How do international privacy laws affect global AEO implementations?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Global AEO implementations must comply with privacy laws in all user jurisdictions, typically requiring implementation of the most restrictive requirements across all markets.</p>
</div>
</section>

